        "original_id": "8212457c-1288-5600-9f9b-863696611155",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Istanbul, Turkey, Ayakapı, Sultanahmet Square, Fatih district\n- Buildings: Gül Mosque, Hippodrome of Constantinople\n- Organizations: Turkish and Islamic Arts Museum\n- Concepts: Eastern Orthodox church, mosque, Byzantine buildings, Ottoman conversion\n\nFacts:\n- Gül Mosque in Istanbul, Turkey, is a former Eastern Orthodox church that the Ottomans converted into a mosque.\n- Ayakapı contains the Gül Mosque, one of the most important surviving Byzantine buildings on Istanbul's historical peninsula.\n- The Hippodrome of Constantinople is today a square called Sultanahmet Square in Istanbul, with only a few fragments of the original structure surviving.\n- The Turkish and Islamic Arts Museum is located in Sultanahmet Square in the Fatih district of Istanbul, Turkey.",
